From d49ee99b0a052a2143fcfd5179f64513eb974972 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: JohnnyC96 <54557697+JohnnyC96@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 17:26:44 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Recomp+Runtime: generated code includes a game-facing API
 header, not ps2_runtime.h

Every generated source included ps2_runtime.h, the runtime's whole interior (GS, memory, VU, audio, pad, VFS, IOP), so any runtime-internal change rebuilt all generated code. New ps2_runtime_api.h declares only what generated code uses: R5900Context, PS2Exception, the function-table types and the ps2x_* entry points (dispatchGuestBranch, eeCheckpointDue, syscall/break/trap/TLB handlers, SignalException, clearLLBit, VU0 microprogram calls, the GIF DMA kick, Load/Store 8-128). The emitters call ps2x_*(runtime, ...); the PS2Runtime members of the same name are inline wrappers. Guest address constants move to runtime/ps2_memory_map.h. Runner PCH uses the API header; main.cpp is kept out of the generated unity batches.
---
